      <a href="#mistakes">Common Mistakes</a>
      <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
    </TableOfContents>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pb-16 lg:pb-24">
      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          Ancient Nutrition protein powder is worth buying if you want dairy-free bone broth protein: Bone Broth Protein Pure lists 20 g of protein in 90 calories and cost about $1.78 per 25 g at the Amazon price we saw. The answer changes for the rest of the range, because Multi Collagen is a 9 g supplement scoop and the whey-based powders cost far more per gram. Here is the full label, testing and price breakdown.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Ancient Nutrition Protein Powder: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            Ancient Nutrition is a good choice for one job: dairy-free protein from bone broth. Its Bone Broth Protein lists 20 g of protein in 90 calories per scoop, and the Pure flavor contains only chicken and beef bone broth protein concentrates. The rest of the range is either a collagen supplement with 9 g of protein per scoop or a whey-based shake that costs two to four times what a standard whey does per gram. None of it carries an NSF Certified for Sport or Informed Sport seal that we could find.
          </p>

          <p>
            <strong>Buy it if</strong> you avoid dairy, eat paleo or simply want a protein you can stir into soup. <strong>Skip it if</strong> your goal is muscle at the lowest cost, you are a tested athlete who needs a certified product, or you have a fish or egg allergy and are looking at Multi Collagen or Multi Protein. If bone broth is the draw, compare it with the other tubs in our <a href="/best-bone-broth-protein-powder/">best bone broth protein powder</a> roundup before you buy.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
